  "notes": "Left strand and PNV differ on form and pace (independence against shared, gradual sovereignty) but agree on the right to decide, the territory, euskera and civic inclusion. The founder's racial and religious doctrine (Arana) contradicts the current texts on ethnic-nation, religious-nation and immigration; those answers follow the current texts and are capped at medium. Searched: nation and territory, sovereignty, language, minorities and newcomers, diaspora, means. Economic, welfare and social-policy statements are null as the coalition's or government's programme. Main gap: Arana's own Obras completas (Bizkaya por su independencia, Larrazabal speech) was not found in full text; his positions come from scholarship that quotes them.",
